<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">20 July in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 20 July, from 792 to 1976.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">792 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,234 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Khan Kardam of Bulgaria defeats Constantine VI at Markellai</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Near the fortress of Markellai, close to present-day Karnobat, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgarians">Bulgarians</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kardam">Khan Kardam</a> routed the Byzantine army of Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantine-vi">Constantine VI</a>, who fled the field. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantium</a> was forced to resume paying tribute to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-markellai">Battle of Markellai</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantine-vi">Constantine VI</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/911">911 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,115 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">A relief army defeats Rollo's Vikings besieging Chartres</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rollo">Rollo</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikings">Vikings</a>, who had besieged <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chartres">Chartres</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-francia">West Francia</a> since spring, were defeated when a relief army arrived. The failure led to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-saint-clair-sur-epte">Treaty of Saint-Clair-sur-Epte</a>, by which King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-the-simple">Charles the Simple</a> granted Rollo lands around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rouen">Rouen</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rollo">Rollo</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1189">1189 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">837 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Richard I is invested as duke of Normandy</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/richard-i-of-england">Richard I</a>, known as the Lionheart, was officially invested as duke of Normandy. He was crowned king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/westminster-abbey">Westminster Abbey</a> on 3 September and became a leading commander of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-crusade">Third Crusade</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/richard-i-of-england">Richard I of England</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1333">1333 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">693 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Berwick-upon-Tweed surrenders to Edward III</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Scottish-held town of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berwick-upon-tweed">Berwick-upon-Tweed</a> surrendered to King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edward-iii-of-england">Edward III of England</a> after a four-month siege, once a Scottish relief army had been heavily defeated at Halidon Hill. The English-backed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edward-balliol">Edward Balliol</a> then established his authority over most of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berwick-upon-tweed">Berwick-upon-Tweed</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edward-iii-of-england">Edward III of England</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-war-of-scottish-independence">Second War of Scottish Independence</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1810">1810 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">216 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Bogotá rises against Spanish rule</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A quarrel over a borrowed flower vase sparked an uprising in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bogota">Bogotá</a> that created a governing junta. Colombia celebrates 20 July as its Independence Day; full independence came after Bolívar's victory in 1819.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1866">1866 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">160 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Austria defeats Italy at Lissa, the first great ironclad battle</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Admiral Tegetthoff's Austrian fleet defeated a larger Italian force off the island of Lissa in the Adriatic. The ramming of the Italian flagship convinced navies to fit rams to warships for decades.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1944">1944 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">82 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Stauffenberg's bomb fails to kill Hitler</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Colonel <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/claus-von-stauffenberg">Claus von Stauffenberg</a> left a briefcase bomb at Hitler's Wolf's Lair headquarters, but Hitler survived. The plotters were executed and thousands more were arrested in the reprisals that followed.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1969">1969 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">57 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Apollo 11 lands on the Moon</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Neil Armstrong and Buzz Aldrin landed the lunar module Eagle in the Sea of Tranquillity. Hours later, at 10.56 pm US Eastern time, Armstrong stepped onto the surface, watched by some 600 million people.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/vikings" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vikings.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1976">1976 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">50 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Viking 1 makes the first successful landing on Mars</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">NASA's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikings">Viking</a> 1 lander touched down on Chryse Planitia and sent back the first photographs from the Martian surface. It operated for more than six years.</p></div></li></ol>
